# The rescued Vadu children in Krezk (NPC plan batch 4; docs/plans/npc_depth_and_quests.md): Ioana and Zamfir, the twins, who
# stay close together (Zamfir was the one who cried in the den, and Ioana says it was her), and Codruta, who lost her rag
# doll on the hillside (she hid it under a gorse root so the wolves wouldn't take it too; if the party found it, she gets
# it back here). They stand in the lanes by day once the pack's children are free (flag den_children_freed). No fight,
# nothing behind a roll. Lines drafted by Gemini through the ai-bridge, edited; every line here is unvoiced for now.

~ ioana
Ioana [smile]: Ma gave us warm milk with lard in it. Do you want half of my bread? It only fell in the snow once.
Narrator: Behind her, a smaller shadow in an identical wool coat clutches two fistfuls of her hem and stares at your boots.
-> ioana_menu

~ ioana_menu
* Who cried, in the den? -> ioana_cried
* Goodbye. -> END

~ ioana_cried
set twins_cry_heard
Ioana: That was me you heard down in the rocks. I have very loud lungs when I'm cross.
Narrator: Beside her, Zamfir keeps both eyes fixed on the mud and says nothing at all, though a small thumb hooks tighter into Ioana's sleeve.
Ioana: I'm older by a whole minute, so it was my turn to make the noise. That's how we do it.
-> ioana_menu

~ zamfir
Zamfir [afraid]: Your cloak smells like wet dog and iron, just like the dark place, only nicer.
Narrator: Having spent all that bravery in a single breath, Zamfir disappears behind Ioana's shoulder again.
-> zamfir_menu

~ zamfir_menu
* [if flag.twins_cry_heard] Ioana says she cried in the den. Was it her? -> zamfir_cried
* Goodbye. -> END

~ zamfir_cried
Zamfir [sly]: I cried the whole time in the dark, right until you came. I was ever so loud.
Ioana [weary]: It was me. I was the loud one, and that is all anyone needs to know. Now hush and eat your crust before the crows get it.
Narrator: Ioana reaches back without looking to tug Zamfir's hood straight, keeping the lie between them like a shared blanket.
-> zamfir_menu

~ codruta
if flag.ana_doll_returned
Narrator: She holds a damp, button-eyed rag doll by the neck with both hands, glaring up at you as if you might ask to borrow it.
Codruta [angry]: Her skirt got torn on the thorns, and she's missing an ear, and nobody is allowed to touch her but me.
else
Narrator: Her mittens are empty, and she keeps opening and closing her fingers as if checking whether something has come back to them.
Codruta [sad]: Linen doesn't have any fur on it. She's going to freeze out there on the hill all by herself.
endif
-> codruta_menu

~ codruta_menu
* [if flag.den_doll_found and not flag.ana_doll_returned] We found your doll on the hillside. -> codruta_returned
* [if not flag.codruta_hid_told] Where did you lose her? -> codruta_hid
* Goodbye. -> END

~ codruta_returned
set ana_doll_returned
Narrator: She holds a damp, button-eyed rag doll by the neck with both hands, glaring up at you as if you might ask to borrow it.
Codruta [angry]: Her skirt got torn on the thorns, and she's missing an ear, and nobody is allowed to touch her but me.
approve thistle +1 kip_smudgewick +1 godrick_pendlebrook +1: You gave Codruta back her rag doll
-> codruta_menu

~ codruta_hid
set codruta_hid_told
Codruta [afraid]: When the big gray one picked me up, I pushed her under the gorse root by the ditch. I didn't drop her.
Narrator: She wipes her nose on her sleeve and looks toward the gate, where the mist presses white against the timber.
Codruta: If the wolves took both of us, there'd be nobody left to know where we lived. So I made her stay behind.
-> codruta_menu
